  "worked_solution": "Here, the denominator is the imaginary number $4\\text{i}.$ Note that this can be written as $0+4\\text{i},$ so the conjugate is $0-4\\text{i},$ or simply $-4\\text{i}.$\n\nSo, we multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $-4\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-12+5\\text{i}}{4\\text{i}} & =\\frac{-12+5\\text{i}}{4\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{-4\\text{i}}{-4\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{48\\text{i}-20{\\text{i}}^{2}}{-16{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{48\\text{i}-20(-1)}{-16(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{20+48\\text{i}}{16}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{20+48\\text{i}}{16} & =\\frac{20}{16}+\\frac{48}{16}\\text{i} \\\\  & =(\\frac{5}{4})+(3)\\,\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
